 ### Merge policy
 
-Three policies are supported. The policy determines what happens at the merge gate (Rail 7).
+Four policies are supported. The policy determines what happens at the merge gate (Rail 7).
 
 | Policy | AUTO tickets | ADJUDICATE tickets | ESCALATE tickets |
 |--------|-------------|-------------------|-----------------|
 | `human` (default) | Human approval required | Human approval required | Human approval required |
 | `auto-low-risk` | Auto-merge after review passes | Human approval required | Human approval required |
 | `auto-after-advisor` | Auto-merge after review passes | Auto-merge after advisor approved + review passes | Auto-merge after advisor approved + review passes |
+| `auto-jev` (shadow) | Human approval required | Human approval required | Human approval required |
+
+`auto-jev` is shadow mode (ADR-0008). Its effective policy is `human`, with the reason
+"auto-jev: shadow mode". Step 2d-jev records a Jev verdict next to the rule bucket. No code path
+reads that verdict to merge, and a rule-based ESCALATE bucket always wins. Gating on the score needs
+a new ADR that supersedes ADR-0008.
 
